{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## A REAL Cloud defect was found by AC4 -- filed, not fixed here\n\n[rebar:cabc-7a98-d173-4d7c] \"Cloud acli_graph readers spin forever on a repeated cursor\ntoken\", linked discovered_from this ticket.\n\nMechanism: if the server returns the SAME non-null nextPageToken with isLast falsy, the\nrequest body is byte-identical each iteration, the response is identical, and neither\nbreak fires -- the loop never terminates. There is no same-token-twice guard and no\nrequest ceiling. fetcher._iter_pages HAS exactly this guard (fetcher.py:286-308,\ntoken_seen_count -> SilentTruncationError(reason=\"same-token-twice\")); these three readers\nare a separate code path with a separate cursor and do not.\n\nSecond-order effect: each reader wraps the POST in a fail-open `except Exception: break`,\nso the spin ends only when the transport finally errors, and that error is swallowed at\nWARNING -- the pass then completes with a SILENTLY PARTIAL map. Same invisible symptom as\nchange 1105 / [rebar:9263-b404-cb6c-463f] / [rebar:deac-4f5a-856a-49bd].\n\nMeasured: 26 requests issued against a token-repeating stub, ending only because the test\nharness raised at its own 25-call cap; the result was a 1-entry map. Without the harness\ncap the call does not return.\n\nPer this ticket's instructions, production behaviour was NOT changed. AC4's oracle is\ntherefore committed as the CONTRACT (the reader must stop on its own within two requests,\nwithout the harness breaking the spin) under xfail(strict=True) citing the bug id:\ntest_a_repeated_cursor_token_stops_the_walk_on_its_own. strict=True means it goes RED the\nmoment the guard lands, forcing conversion to a plain assertion -- so the xfail cannot rot\ninto permanent silence. AC4's \"pins which\" is answered explicitly: today it does NEITHER\n(no raise, no stop); the pin is on the correct behaviour plus the filed defect.\n\n## Gates\n\n  * module sizes: acli_graph.py 606 -> 606 (unchanged; no production edit landed);\n    new test module 521 lines. Nothing near the 800 cap.\n  * ruff check + ruff format --check + mypy clean; pre-commit gate passed on commit.\n  * docs/env-vars.md not affected (no env reads added).\n  * targeted runs only: the new module, mutate/test_acli_cross_mixin_binding.py, and\n    test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py -- 52 passed, 1 xfailed.\n  * files touched: exactly one new test file. adapters/jira/** read-only."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785720640587969001,"uuid":"ef1d8a26-4f65-4c5e-b92b-1353677c7d10"}